1
00:00:01,340 --> 00:00:01,390
Four and a half billion dollars.

2
00:00:01,440 --> 00:00:05,150
That's how much Finder estimates
Australians spend on Black Friday.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,050
And this year,

4
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:09,630
Black Friday lands on the
27th of November 2026,

5
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:11,630
with Cyber Monday on the 30th.

6
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:15,190
For years, Black Friday was
about TVs, phones and air fryers.

7
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:15,780
Not anymore.

8
00:00:15,830 --> 00:00:17,710
Car brands have jumped in.

9
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:21,020
Last November, Suzuki,
Omoda Jaecoo, Geely,

10
00:00:21,070 --> 00:00:25,810
Chery and Isuzu all ran Black Friday
car deals in Australia cashback,

11
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:29,210
free servicing, cheap finance,
thousands off drive-away prices.

12
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:30,870
But here's the problem.

13
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:33,270
When Savvy looked at last
year's Black Friday car sales,

14
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:36,930
it found that at least one big brand's
"Black Friday" campaign was really just

15
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:38,150
a demo clearance.

16
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:41,445
And some of the cheapest-looking finance
offers came with deposits of up to

17
00:00:41,495 --> 00:00:44,490
thirty-five per cent, or a big
balloon payment at the end.

18
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:45,350
So in this video,

19
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:48,450
I'm going to show you what car
deals are on the table right now,

20
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:51,870
why 2026 could be the biggest
year yet for discounting,

21
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:53,830
the traps that cost buyers thousands,

22
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:57,510
and exactly how to tell a real
Black Friday deal from a fake one.

23
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:59,550
Because a car isn't a toaster.

24
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:02,620
Get this wrong, and you could pay
for it for the next five years.

25
00:01:03,314 --> 00:01:06,604
First, let's be clear about
what we know, and what we don't.

26
00:01:06,654 --> 00:01:07,824
As I record this,

27
00:01:07,874 --> 00:01:11,704
most car brands haven't announced
their 2026 Black Friday deals yet.

28
00:01:11,754 --> 00:01:14,104
They usually land in the
second half of November.

29
00:01:14,154 --> 00:01:16,944
So I'm not going to invent
offers that don't exist.

30
00:01:16,994 --> 00:01:19,384
Instead, I'll show you
what happened last year,

31
00:01:19,434 --> 00:01:23,044
what's being offered right now, and
what to watch for when the deals drop.

32
00:01:23,094 --> 00:01:26,924
Let's start with 2025, because
it tells us what to expect.

33
00:01:26,974 --> 00:01:28,744
Suzuki ran a short Black Friday sale,

34
00:01:28,794 --> 00:01:31,624
from the 21st to the 23rd of November,

35
00:01:31,674 --> 00:01:34,274
with one thousand dollars
cashback on the Vitara,

36
00:01:34,324 --> 00:01:36,751
S-Cross and Ignis, while stocks lasted.

37
00:01:36,801 --> 00:01:41,004
Omoda Jaecoo offered two thousand
dollars cashback plus three years of free

38
00:01:41,054 --> 00:01:43,744
scheduled servicing across the Jaecoo J7,

39
00:01:43,794 --> 00:01:50,364
the J8 and the Omoda 9, with the J7
starting from $32,990 drive-away.

40
00:01:50,414 --> 00:01:51,904
Geely offered gift cards,

41
00:01:51,954 --> 00:01:56,284
free charging cables and cheap finance
on the EX5 and the Starray EM-i.

42
00:01:56,334 --> 00:01:59,424
Chery offered two thousand
dollars off selected models.

43
00:01:59,474 --> 00:02:00,731
And according to Savvy,

44
00:02:00,781 --> 00:02:04,144
Isuzu advertised drive-away discounts
of between five and eight thousand

45
00:02:04,194 --> 00:02:06,964
dollars on the D-Max ute and the MU-X.

46
00:02:07,014 --> 00:02:09,104
And the year before, in 2024,

47
00:02:09,154 --> 00:02:12,164
the deals were even bigger
on some slow-selling models.

48
00:02:12,214 --> 00:02:16,924
Skoda took ten thousand dollars off the
last 135 Superb Sportline sedans and

49
00:02:16,974 --> 00:02:17,944
wagons.

50
00:02:17,994 --> 00:02:22,084
Mazda cut nearly ten thousand
dollars from selected CX-60 variants.

51
00:02:22,134 --> 00:02:25,684
BYD took three thousand dollars off
most of its range and threw in a wall

52
00:02:25,734 --> 00:02:28,484
charger, although
installation wasn't included.

53
00:02:28,534 --> 00:02:31,084
And Suzuki offered ten
per cent off its range,

54
00:02:31,134 --> 00:02:34,164
including the Jimny but only
on cars already in stock,

55
00:02:34,214 --> 00:02:37,004
and with delivery required
by the 30th of November.

56
00:02:37,054 --> 00:02:38,024
Notice something?

57
00:02:38,074 --> 00:02:40,344
Most of those deals came
from Chinese brands,

58
00:02:40,394 --> 00:02:42,764
or from brands fighting to
hold on to market share.

59
00:02:42,814 --> 00:02:44,944
And most of them weren't
simple price cuts.

60
00:02:44,994 --> 00:02:48,804
They were cashback, gift cards,
free servicing or finance deals.

61
00:02:48,854 --> 00:02:51,154
That matters, and I'll explain why later.

62
00:02:51,912 --> 00:02:54,482
So why could 2026 be even bigger?

63
00:02:54,532 --> 00:02:56,782
Reason one: competition.

64
00:02:56,832 --> 00:03:00,702
Australia now has around seventy car
brands fighting for about 1.2 million

65
00:03:00,752 --> 00:03:02,062
sales a year.

66
00:03:02,112 --> 00:03:03,942
New Chinese brands keep arriving,

67
00:03:03,992 --> 00:03:06,182
and they're using price
as their main weapon.

68
00:03:06,232 --> 00:03:07,942
In September 2026,

69
00:03:07,992 --> 00:03:13,782
BYD sold 8,191 cars and was the second
best-selling brand in the country.

70
00:03:13,832 --> 00:03:16,122
GWM is pushing towards the top five.

71
00:03:16,172 --> 00:03:18,662
To keep up, everyone else
has to sharpen their pencil.

72
00:03:18,712 --> 00:03:22,002
Reason two: the government's
New Vehicle Efficiency Standard.

73
00:03:22,052 --> 00:03:23,575
Since July 2025,

74
00:03:23,625 --> 00:03:27,922
car makers whose fleets produce too
much carbon dioxide face penalties.

75
00:03:27,972 --> 00:03:30,182
In the first six months alone,

76
00:03:30,232 --> 00:03:34,582
Mazda's liability was estimated
at around $25.4 million,

77
00:03:34,632 --> 00:03:37,242
Nissan's at around $10.7 million,

78
00:03:37,292 --> 00:03:41,982
Subaru's at almost $7 million and
Hyundai's at about $4.2 million.

79
00:03:42,032 --> 00:03:46,502
Meanwhile, BYD, Toyota and Tesla
built up millions of credits.

80
00:03:46,552 --> 00:03:49,322
And in 2026, the targets get tighter.

81
00:03:49,372 --> 00:03:52,882
That gives brands a big reason to push
electric and hybrid cars out of the

82
00:03:52,932 --> 00:03:55,942
door and discounting is
the fastest way to do it.

83
00:03:55,992 --> 00:03:57,062
Hyundai, for example,

84
00:03:57,112 --> 00:04:03,042
cut up to $13,857 from some versions
of the Kona Electric earlier this year.

85
00:04:03,092 --> 00:04:06,482
And the government's Clean Energy Finance
Corporation committed sixty million

86
00:04:06,532 --> 00:04:08,542
dollars to Hyundai Capital Australia,

87
00:04:08,592 --> 00:04:13,102
to support discounted interest rates
on Hyundai and Kia electric cars.

88
00:04:13,152 --> 00:04:16,582
At the same time, the cheap end
of the EV market has exploded.

89
00:04:16,632 --> 00:04:18,092
In February 2026,

90
00:04:18,142 --> 00:04:22,286
CarsGuide listed seven electric cars
available for under forty thousand

91
00:04:22,336 --> 00:04:24,492
dollars drive-away,
including the BYD Dolphin,

92
00:04:24,542 --> 00:04:27,422
the BYD Atto 2, the MG4,

93
00:04:27,472 --> 00:04:32,702
the GWM Ora, the Chery E5, the
Leapmotor B10 and the Hyundai Inster.

94
00:04:32,752 --> 00:04:35,489
A few years ago, that list
would have been almost empty.

95
00:04:35,539 --> 00:04:37,062
Reason three: fuel.

96
00:04:37,112 --> 00:04:40,502
With petrol and diesel
prices high in 2026,

97
00:04:40,552 --> 00:04:43,682
more buyers are looking at hybrids
and EVs, and brands know it.

98
00:04:43,732 --> 00:04:47,282
That's why you're now seeing fuel cards
offered as a sweetener on petrol cars

99
00:04:47,332 --> 00:04:48,182
too.

100
00:04:48,232 --> 00:04:53,462
In 2025, battery electric cars made up
about 8.3 per cent of new car sales.

101
00:04:53,512 --> 00:04:57,902
By September 2026, it was more than
twenty-four per cent in a single month.

102
00:04:57,952 --> 00:05:00,242
That's a massive shift
in a very short time.

103
00:05:00,292 --> 00:05:02,382
And reason four: the calendar.

104
00:05:02,432 --> 00:05:05,922
Black Friday is the last big sales
event before the end of the year.

105
00:05:05,972 --> 00:05:07,442
And on the 1st of January,

106
00:05:07,492 --> 00:05:12,062
every unsold 2026-built car becomes,
in the eyes of buyers, a year older.

107
00:05:12,112 --> 00:05:15,092
Dealers want those cars
gone before that happens.

108
00:05:15,971 --> 00:05:18,681
So what's on offer right
now, heading into November?

109
00:05:18,731 --> 00:05:22,441
Here's what CarsGuide
reported in October 2026.

110
00:05:22,491 --> 00:05:27,081
GWM was celebrating eighteen years in
Australia with cuts across its range.

111
00:05:27,131 --> 00:05:32,061
The Haval Jolion Premium was down
three thousand dollars to $23,990

112
00:05:32,111 --> 00:05:33,181
drive-away.

113
00:05:33,231 --> 00:05:39,261
The Haval H6 hybrid Lux was
$37,990, three thousand dollars off.

114
00:05:39,311 --> 00:05:42,521
And the Cannon Alpha diesel Ultra
ute was four thousand dollars off,

115
00:05:42,571 --> 00:05:45,221
at $54,990.

116
00:05:45,271 --> 00:05:48,441
Those deals were advertised
until the 31st of October.

117
00:05:48,491 --> 00:05:52,801
Chery offered three thousand dollars
cashback on the Tiggo 8 plug-in hybrid,

118
00:05:52,851 --> 00:05:55,801
now $42,990 drive-away,

119
00:05:55,851 --> 00:06:01,241
and on the seven-seat Tiggo 9 plug-in
hybrid, now $49,990 drive-away.

120
00:06:01,291 --> 00:06:04,941
It also offered fuel cards worth up
to two thousand dollars on other Tiggo

121
00:06:04,991 --> 00:06:06,061
models.

122
00:06:06,111 --> 00:06:08,501
Geely offered six per cent off the EX2,

123
00:06:08,551 --> 00:06:12,921
EX5 and Starray EM-i but only
for buyers using a novated lease,

124
00:06:12,971 --> 00:06:15,081
and before on-road costs.

125
00:06:15,131 --> 00:06:16,221
At the premium end,

126
00:06:16,271 --> 00:06:21,921
Mercedes-Benz advertised the
GLC 200 from $79,990 drive-away,

127
00:06:21,971 --> 00:06:26,141
compared with a price of around
$89,000 before on-road costs,

128
00:06:26,191 --> 00:06:29,761
as long as you order by the 30th of
November and take delivery before the end

129
00:06:29,811 --> 00:06:30,681
of the year.

130
00:06:30,731 --> 00:06:36,641
And Skoda was offering the Kodiaq mild
hybrid from $49,990 drive-away until

131
00:06:36,691 --> 00:06:40,161
the end of December effectively
covering the on-road costs.

132
00:06:40,211 --> 00:06:41,641
Now, these aren't Black Friday deals.

133
00:06:41,691 --> 00:06:44,441
Many of them ended on the 31st of October.

134
00:06:44,491 --> 00:06:46,401
But they show you the starting point.

135
00:06:46,451 --> 00:06:50,241
If a brand's "Black Friday price" in
late November is the same as its October

136
00:06:50,291 --> 00:06:52,661
price, that's not a Black Friday deal.

137
00:06:52,711 --> 00:06:53,911
That's just the price.

138
00:06:54,773 --> 00:06:56,963
Quick favour before we get to the traps.

139
00:06:57,013 --> 00:06:59,763
If you're planning to buy a
car in the Black Friday sales,

140
00:06:59,813 --> 00:07:01,943
tell me in the comments
which car you're looking at.

141
00:07:01,993 --> 00:07:05,623
I'll keep an eye on the deals and might
cover the best ones in a future video.

142
00:07:05,673 --> 00:07:09,523
And if you want honest, fact-checked
car news for Australia, hit subscribe.

143
00:07:09,573 --> 00:07:12,313
It's free, and it helps the
channel more than you know.

144
00:07:13,055 --> 00:07:14,025
Now, the traps.

145
00:07:14,075 --> 00:07:19,065
And trap number one is the oldest
trick in retail: the fake "was" price.

146
00:07:19,115 --> 00:07:21,925
The ACCC watches Black Friday closely.

147
00:07:21,975 --> 00:07:23,705
After the 2024 sales,

148
00:07:23,755 --> 00:07:26,065
it issued infringement
notices to Michael Hill,

149
00:07:26,115 --> 00:07:29,665
MyHouse and Hairhouse
Online, totalling $59,400,

150
00:07:29,715 --> 00:07:35,085
over "sitewide" sale ads that the
ACCC alleged excluded some products.

151
00:07:35,135 --> 00:07:37,905
Those weren't car companies,
but the lesson is the same.

152
00:07:37,955 --> 00:07:41,785
A big "save" number only means something
if the "before" price was real.

153
00:07:41,835 --> 00:07:44,185
With cars, the trick
usually looks different.

154
00:07:44,235 --> 00:07:47,625
A dealer might compare the drive-away
price with the manufacturer's list price

155
00:07:47,675 --> 00:07:49,345
before on-road costs.

156
00:07:49,395 --> 00:07:52,625
Or compare it with a price nobody
has actually paid for months.

157
00:07:52,675 --> 00:07:53,925
So before Black Friday,

158
00:07:53,975 --> 00:07:56,825
write down the drive-away price
of the car you want today.

159
00:07:56,875 --> 00:07:59,085
Then compare it with
the Black Friday price.

160
00:07:59,135 --> 00:08:00,545
That's your real saving.

161
00:08:00,595 --> 00:08:02,765
And here's something a lot
of buyers don't realise.

162
00:08:02,815 --> 00:08:06,085
There's a big difference between a
"drive-away" price and a price "before

163
00:08:06,135 --> 00:08:07,235
on-road costs".

164
00:08:07,285 --> 00:08:10,245
On-road costs include
things like stamp duty,

165
00:08:10,295 --> 00:08:14,325
registration, compulsory third
party insurance and dealer charges.

166
00:08:14,375 --> 00:08:16,365
Depending on the car and
the state you live in,

167
00:08:16,415 --> 00:08:18,125
they can add thousands of dollars.

168
00:08:18,175 --> 00:08:21,745
So a deal advertised before on-road
costs can look much cheaper than a

169
00:08:21,795 --> 00:08:23,785
drive-away deal that's actually better.

170
00:08:23,835 --> 00:08:26,125
Always compare drive-away with drive-away.

171
00:08:26,175 --> 00:08:29,225
And even an advertised drive-away
price isn't set in stone.

172
00:08:29,275 --> 00:08:32,525
You can still ask for a breakdown
of it, and you can still negotiate.

173
00:08:32,575 --> 00:08:36,285
A Black Friday price is the dealer's
opening offer, not the final word.

174
00:08:36,335 --> 00:08:41,085
Trap number two: the demo or
runout car dressed up as a sale.

175
00:08:41,135 --> 00:08:43,925
When Savvy reviewed last
year's Black Friday car deals,

176
00:08:43,975 --> 00:08:47,765
its managing editor Thomas Perrotta
warned that "some manufacturers may just

177
00:08:47,815 --> 00:08:48,725
be selling demo,

178
00:08:48,775 --> 00:08:53,245
runout or plate clearance models." A
demo can be a great buy but only if it's

179
00:08:53,295 --> 00:08:57,025
priced like a used car, because it's
already been registered and driven.

180
00:08:57,075 --> 00:08:58,825
Always ask how many kilometres it has,

181
00:08:58,875 --> 00:09:01,795
when it was first registered,
and when the warranty started.

182
00:09:02,552 --> 00:09:05,562
Trap number three is the big one: finance.

183
00:09:05,612 --> 00:09:09,142
You'll see headlines like
"finance from 1.99 per cent".

184
00:09:09,192 --> 00:09:12,952
Savvy warned that these low-rate
deals often come with short terms of

185
00:09:13,002 --> 00:09:14,962
thirty-six to forty-eight months,

186
00:09:15,012 --> 00:09:19,322
deposits of up to thirty-five per cent,
or a large balloon payment at the end.

187
00:09:19,372 --> 00:09:21,182
On a fifty-thousand-dollar car,

188
00:09:21,232 --> 00:09:24,822
Savvy estimated repayments
could be more than $490 a week,

189
00:09:24,872 --> 00:09:28,402
or about $2,125 a month.

190
00:09:28,452 --> 00:09:33,082
As Perrotta put it: "The devil is in
the details." And there's another catch.

191
00:09:33,132 --> 00:09:36,402
If you apply for dealer finance and
don't qualify for the advertised rate,

192
00:09:36,452 --> 00:09:40,462
you might be offered a standard five-year
loan at a much higher rate Savvy

193
00:09:40,512 --> 00:09:44,622
said often at or above ten per cent
after a credit enquiry has already been

194
00:09:44,672 --> 00:09:45,802
made on your file.

195
00:09:45,852 --> 00:09:48,258
To see why this matters,
let's do some simple maths.

196
00:09:48,308 --> 00:09:51,842
Borrow forty thousand dollars
over five years at seven per cent,

197
00:09:51,892 --> 00:09:58,662
and you'll pay about $792 a
month, or around $47,500 in total.

198
00:09:58,712 --> 00:10:00,442
Borrow the same amount at ten per cent,

199
00:10:00,492 --> 00:10:05,442
and it's about $850 a month
roughly $51,000 in total.

200
00:10:05,492 --> 00:10:07,702
That's around three and a
half thousand dollars more,

201
00:10:07,752 --> 00:10:10,462
which can easily wipe out
a Black Friday discount.

202
00:10:10,512 --> 00:10:11,662
So here's what to do.

203
00:10:11,712 --> 00:10:15,342
Get pre-approved for a car loan from
your bank or a broker before Black

204
00:10:15,392 --> 00:10:16,082
Friday.

205
00:10:16,132 --> 00:10:18,542
Then you can compare the
dealer's offer properly.

206
00:10:18,592 --> 00:10:22,082
Always compare the comparison
rate, not just the headline rate.

207
00:10:22,132 --> 00:10:22,902
Ask about the balloon.

208
00:10:22,952 --> 00:10:26,882
And work out the total amount you'll
pay over the life of the loan not just

209
00:10:26,932 --> 00:10:28,402
the weekly repayment.

210
00:10:28,452 --> 00:10:31,582
Savvy also warned about one more
thing that catches people out:

211
00:10:31,632 --> 00:10:34,902
using buy now, pay later
on Black Friday shopping.

212
00:10:34,952 --> 00:10:38,022
Lenders can see it, and it can
hurt your car loan application.

213
00:10:38,072 --> 00:10:41,972
So if you're planning to buy a car, go
easy on the other Black Friday sales.

214
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:46,851
Trap number four: the sweetener
that's worth less than it looks.

215
00:10:46,901 --> 00:10:49,331
Cashback, gift cards, fuel cards,

216
00:10:49,381 --> 00:10:52,391
free servicing and free
accessories all sound great.

217
00:10:52,441 --> 00:10:53,811
And sometimes they are.

218
00:10:53,861 --> 00:10:56,711
Three years of free
servicing on a Jaecoo J7,

219
00:10:56,761 --> 00:10:59,951
for example, was worth around
nine hundred dollars last year.

220
00:11:00,001 --> 00:11:03,911
But a fuel card or a gift card is
not the same as money off the price.

221
00:11:03,961 --> 00:11:09,411
In 2024, BYD's Black Friday deal
included a free wall charger valued at a

222
00:11:09,461 --> 00:11:12,211
thousand dollars but
installation wasn't included,

223
00:11:12,261 --> 00:11:14,871
and installing a charger
can cost hundreds more.

224
00:11:14,921 --> 00:11:18,751
And some of these extras come with
conditions a certain finance company,

225
00:11:18,801 --> 00:11:21,931
a certain delivery date, or no
other offers allowed on top.

226
00:11:21,981 --> 00:11:23,031
A simple rule:

227
00:11:23,081 --> 00:11:27,071
always ask the dealer what the drive-away
price would be without the extras.

228
00:11:27,121 --> 00:11:30,711
Sometimes you'll get a bigger saving
by negotiating the price down instead.

229
00:11:30,761 --> 00:11:33,831
Trap number five: the delivery deadline.

230
00:11:33,881 --> 00:11:37,871
Many Black Friday car offers say the
car must be delivered by a certain date

231
00:11:37,921 --> 00:11:41,351
often the 30th of November
or the 31st of December.

232
00:11:41,401 --> 00:11:44,251
If the car you want isn't in
stock and has to be shipped,

233
00:11:44,301 --> 00:11:46,171
ask what happens if it arrives late.

234
00:11:46,221 --> 00:11:47,531
Do you still get the deal?

235
00:11:47,581 --> 00:11:49,491
Get the answer in
writing on your contract,

236
00:11:49,541 --> 00:11:51,751
not just a verbal promise
from the salesperson.

237
00:11:51,801 --> 00:11:53,531
And be careful with deposits.

238
00:11:53,581 --> 00:11:56,371
If you pay a deposit to lock
in a Black Friday price,

239
00:11:56,421 --> 00:11:59,151
ask whether it's refundable,
and under what conditions.

240
00:11:59,201 --> 00:12:00,751
As we saw with the Cybertruck,

241
00:12:00,801 --> 00:12:03,991
a deposit is only as good
as the paperwork behind it.

242
00:12:04,041 --> 00:12:06,691
Trap number six: deals that
are tied to someone else.

243
00:12:06,741 --> 00:12:10,411
Last year, some of the best-looking
offers like three thousand dollars

244
00:12:10,461 --> 00:12:14,871
cashback on BYD models through Savvy
were only available if you took out a car

245
00:12:14,921 --> 00:12:16,731
loan through that particular broker.

246
00:12:16,781 --> 00:12:18,431
That can still be a good deal.

247
00:12:18,481 --> 00:12:20,751
Just make sure the loan
itself is competitive,

248
00:12:20,801 --> 00:12:23,821
because a cheap car with an
expensive loan isn't cheap.

249
00:12:24,624 --> 00:12:27,034
Now, if you're thinking
about an electric car,

250
00:12:27,084 --> 00:12:30,094
there's one more date you need to know
and it has nothing to do with Black

251
00:12:30,144 --> 00:12:30,954
Friday.

252
00:12:31,004 --> 00:12:34,714
Right now, electric cars bought through
a novated lease can be exempt from

253
00:12:34,764 --> 00:12:36,134
fringe benefits tax,

254
00:12:36,184 --> 00:12:39,354
as long as they're under the luxury
car tax threshold for fuel-efficient

255
00:12:39,404 --> 00:12:43,454
vehicles, currently $91,387.

256
00:12:43,504 --> 00:12:45,694
That's called the Electric Car Discount,

257
00:12:45,744 --> 00:12:48,394
and it can save some buyers
thousands of dollars a year.

258
00:12:48,444 --> 00:12:52,094
But in May 2026, the government
confirmed it's being wound back.

259
00:12:52,144 --> 00:12:56,714
The full exemption continues
until the 31st of March 2027.

260
00:12:56,764 --> 00:12:58,894
From the 1st of April 2027,

261
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:02,934
only EVs costing $75,000 or
less keep the full exemption,

262
00:13:02,984 --> 00:13:07,134
while more expensive EVs get a
twenty-five per cent discount instead.

263
00:13:07,184 --> 00:13:09,354
Existing leases are protected.

264
00:13:09,404 --> 00:13:13,374
And remember, plug-in hybrids already
lost the exemption on the 1st of April

265
00:13:13,424 --> 00:13:14,614
2025.

266
00:13:14,664 --> 00:13:18,954
So if you're looking at an EV
over $75,000 on a novated lease,

267
00:13:19,004 --> 00:13:21,154
the timing matters more
than any Black Friday sale.

268
00:13:21,204 --> 00:13:25,364
Talk to your employer and your lease
provider about the dates before you sign.

269
00:13:26,121 --> 00:13:28,671
So how do you actually get a
good deal this Black Friday?

270
00:13:28,721 --> 00:13:30,091
Here's my checklist.

271
00:13:30,141 --> 00:13:33,031
Step one: decide on the
car before the sales start.

272
00:13:33,081 --> 00:13:36,211
Know the model, the variant
and the colours you'd accept.

273
00:13:36,261 --> 00:13:38,831
Black Friday is designed
to make you buy on impulse.

274
00:13:38,881 --> 00:13:39,831
Don't let it.

275
00:13:39,881 --> 00:13:43,511
Step two: record today's drive-away
price from at least three dealers,

276
00:13:43,561 --> 00:13:44,591
in writing.

277
00:13:44,641 --> 00:13:45,351
That's your benchmark.

278
00:13:45,401 --> 00:13:47,331
And ask each one for the breakdown,

279
00:13:47,381 --> 00:13:50,731
so you can see what's the
car and what's on-road costs.

280
00:13:50,781 --> 00:13:52,731
Step three: get finance pre-approved,

281
00:13:52,781 --> 00:13:55,761
and compare comparison
rates, not headline rates.

282
00:13:55,811 --> 00:13:59,511
Step four: when the deal
drops, read the fine print.

283
00:13:59,561 --> 00:14:02,011
Is it for new cars only, or demos too?

284
00:14:02,061 --> 00:14:03,751
Does it end on a specific date?

285
00:14:03,801 --> 00:14:06,191
Does the car have to be delivered
by the 30th of November,

286
00:14:06,241 --> 00:14:08,351
or the 31st of December?

287
00:14:08,401 --> 00:14:10,211
Is it limited to stock on hand?

288
00:14:10,261 --> 00:14:12,331
Step five: ask for the build date.

289
00:14:12,381 --> 00:14:14,591
As we saw with BYD earlier this year,

290
00:14:14,641 --> 00:14:17,131
a car's build date
affects its resale value.

291
00:14:17,181 --> 00:14:21,651
A car built in 2026 and sold in December
will be a year older on paper just

292
00:14:21,701 --> 00:14:22,851
weeks later.

293
00:14:22,901 --> 00:14:24,581
That's fine if the discount reflects it.

294
00:14:24,631 --> 00:14:27,371
Step six: keep the trade-in separate.

295
00:14:27,421 --> 00:14:30,991
Get a written price for the new car
first, then talk about your trade-in.

296
00:14:31,041 --> 00:14:34,951
Otherwise, a big discount on one side
can quietly disappear on the other.

297
00:14:35,001 --> 00:14:37,071
Step seven: check the boring stuff.

298
00:14:37,121 --> 00:14:38,571
How much will servicing cost?

299
00:14:38,621 --> 00:14:39,791
How long is the warranty?

300
00:14:39,841 --> 00:14:41,451
Is there a recall on the model?

301
00:14:41,501 --> 00:14:44,651
You can check recalls on the
Product Safety Australia website.

302
00:14:44,701 --> 00:14:47,611
And remember, a sale price
doesn't reduce your rights.

303
00:14:47,661 --> 00:14:49,051
Under the Australian Consumer Law,

304
00:14:49,101 --> 00:14:53,111
a car bought on Black Friday has exactly
the same consumer guarantees as one

305
00:14:53,161 --> 00:14:54,631
bought at full price.

306
00:14:54,681 --> 00:14:56,411
If it turns out to have a major fault,

307
00:14:56,461 --> 00:15:00,471
the discount doesn't change your right
to a repair, a replacement or a refund.

308
00:15:00,521 --> 00:15:03,531
We covered how that works in
our video on faulty new cars.

309
00:15:03,581 --> 00:15:05,871
And step eight: be ready to walk away.

310
00:15:05,921 --> 00:15:08,251
Black Friday ends, but car deals don't.

311
00:15:08,301 --> 00:15:10,651
The end of December is
often another big push,

312
00:15:10,701 --> 00:15:12,791
as dealers chase year-end targets.

313
00:15:12,841 --> 00:15:15,101
If the deal isn't right,
there'll be another one.

314
00:15:15,790 --> 00:15:18,000
So which brands are
most likely to discount?

315
00:15:18,050 --> 00:15:20,840
Nobody can say for sure until
the deals are announced.

316
00:15:20,890 --> 00:15:23,480
But it's worth watching the
brands under the most pressure.

317
00:15:23,530 --> 00:15:25,640
The ones with emissions
penalties to manage,

318
00:15:25,690 --> 00:15:28,660
like Mazda, Nissan, Subaru and Hyundai.

319
00:15:28,710 --> 00:15:30,800
The Chinese brands
fighting for market share,

320
00:15:30,850 --> 00:15:34,300
like GWM, Chery, Geely and Omoda Jaecoo.

321
00:15:34,350 --> 00:15:36,660
And any brand with a new
model about to arrive,

322
00:15:36,710 --> 00:15:39,040
because the outgoing
model has to be cleared.

323
00:15:39,090 --> 00:15:40,500
If you're flexible on the brand,

324
00:15:40,550 --> 00:15:42,480
that's where the biggest
savings are likely to be.

325
00:15:42,530 --> 00:15:47,220
So, are Black Friday car deals
worth it in Australia in 2026?

326
00:15:47,270 --> 00:15:48,120
They can be.

327
00:15:48,170 --> 00:15:49,440
The market is crowded,

328
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:51,200
Chinese brands are cutting prices,

329
00:15:51,250 --> 00:15:53,540
emissions rules are
pushing EVs and hybrids,

330
00:15:53,590 --> 00:15:57,180
and dealers want 2026-built
stock gone before January.

331
00:15:57,230 --> 00:15:58,920
That's a great setup for buyers.

332
00:15:58,970 --> 00:16:01,640
But a Black Friday banner
doesn't make a deal good.

333
00:16:01,690 --> 00:16:04,940
The real saving is the difference
between the price you could get today and

334
00:16:04,990 --> 00:16:07,760
the price you pay on the
day including the finance.

335
00:16:07,810 --> 00:16:09,740
If this video helped, hit like,

336
00:16:09,790 --> 00:16:12,820
subscribe and share it with
someone who's about to buy a car.

337
00:16:12,870 --> 00:16:16,140
Tell me in the comments which car
you're hoping gets a Black Friday deal.

338
00:16:16,190 --> 00:16:18,640
And when the official 2026 deals land,

339
00:16:18,690 --> 00:16:20,820
I'll be checking which
ones are actually worth it.

340
00:16:20,870 --> 00:16:21,950
See you in the next one.
